{"task_id": "HumanEval/1", "solution": "def separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\" Input to this function is a string containing multiple groups of nested parentheses. Your goal is to\n    separate those group into separate strings and return the list of those.\n    Separate groups are balanced (each open brace is properly closed) and not nested within each other\n    Ignore any spaces in the input string.\n    >>> separate_paren_groups('( ) (( )) (( )( ))')\n    ['()', '(())', '(()())']\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Remove all spaces from the input string.\n    cleaned_string = paren_string.replace(' ', '')\n\n    groups = []\n    balance = 0\n    current_group_start = 0\n\n    # Iterate through the cleaned string to find balanced groups.\n    for i, char in enumerate(cleaned_string):\n        if char == '(':\n            balance += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            balance -= 1\n\n        # If balance returns to 0, a complete, balanced group has been found.\n        if balance == 0:\n            groups.append(cleaned_string[current_group_start : i + 1])\n            current_group_start = i + 1\n            \n    return groups"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/1", "solution": "def separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\" Input to this function is a string containing multiple groups of nested parentheses. Your goal is to\n    separate those group into separate strings and return the list of those.\n    Separate groups are balanced (each open brace is properly closed) and not nested within each other\n    Ignore any spaces in the input string.\n    >>> separate_paren_groups('( ) (( )) (( )( ))')\n    ['()', '(())', '(()())']\n    \"\"\"\n    cleaned_string = paren_string.replace(' ', '')\n    \n    result = []\n    balance = 0\n    current_group_start = 0\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(cleaned_string):\n        if char == '(':\n            balance += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            balance -= 1\n        \n        if balance < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Unbalanced parentheses\")\n        \n        # A group ends when balance returns to 0\n        if balance == 0 and i >= current_group_start:\n            # Only add if it's not an empty string group from start\n            if i - current_group_start + 1 > 0:\n                result.append(cleaned_string[current_group_start : i + 1])\n            current_group_start = i + 1\n            \n    if balance != 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Unbalanced parentheses\")\n        \n    return result"}
