{"task_id": "HumanEval/10", "solution": "```python\ndef make_palindrome(string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\" Find the shortest palindrome that begins with a supplied string.\n    Algorithm idea is simple:\n    - Find the longest postfix of supplied string that is a palindrome.\n    - Append to the end of the string reverse of a string prefix that comes before the palindromic suffix.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    def is_palindrome(s: str) -> bool:\n        return s == s[::-1]\n\n    # Find the longest postfix of the supplied string that is a palindrome.\n    # The loop iterates from the beginning, checking suffixes starting at `i`.\n    # When `is_palindrome(string[i:])` is true, `string[i:]` is the longest palindromic suffix.\n    for i in range(len(string)):\n        if is_palindrome(string[i:]):\n            # The prefix that comes before the palindromic suffix is `string[:i]`.\n            # Append its reverse to the original string.\n            return string + string[:i][::-1]\n    \n    # This case should theoretically not be reached if string is non-empty,\n    # as an empty string (i=len(string)) is a palindrome, and a single character\n    # string (i=len(string)-1) is a palindrome.\n    return string\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/10", "solution": "```python\ndef make_palindrome(string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\" Find the shortest palindrome that begins with a supplied string. \"\"\"\n    if not string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    for i in range(len(string), 0, -1):\n        suffix = string[:i]\n        if suffix == suffix[::-1]:\n            return string + string[i:][::-1]\n    return string + string[::-1]\n```"}
