{"task_id": "HumanEval/19", "solution": "def sort_numbers(numbers: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Input is a space-delimited string of numberals from 'zero' to 'nine'.\n    Return the string with numbers sorted from smallest to largest.\"\"\"\n    number_word_to_int = {\n        \"zero\": 0, \"one\": 1, \"two\": 2, \"three\": 3, \"four\": 4,\n        \"five\": 5, \"six\": 6, \"seven\": 7, \"eight\": 8, \"nine\": 9\n    }\n    int_to_number_word = [\n        \"zero\", \"one\", \"two\", \"three\", \"four\",\n        \"five\", \"six\", \"seven\", \"eight\", \"nine\"\n    ]\n\n    if not numbers.strip():\n        return \"\"\n\n    words = numbers.split()\n    \n    # Convert words to integers\n    nums = [number_word_to_int[word] for word in words]\n    \n    # Sort the integers\n    nums.sort()\n    \n    # Convert sorted integers back to words\n    sorted_words = [int_to_number_word[num] for num in nums]\n    \n    return \" \".join(sorted_words)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/19", "solution": "from typing import List\n\n\ndef sort_numbers(numbers: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a space-delimited string of number words ('zero' to 'nine') from smallest to largest.\n    Converts words to integers, sorts them, then converts back to words.\"\"\"\n\n    # Mappings from number words to integers and vice versa\n    word_to_int = {\n        'zero': 0, 'one': 1, 'two': 2, 'three': 3, 'four': 4,\n        'five': 5, 'six': 6, 'seven': 7, 'eight': 8, 'nine': 9\n    }\n    int_to_word = {v: k for k, v in word_to_int.items()}\n\n    # Split the input string into individual number words\n    words = numbers.split()\n\n    # Convert words to their corresponding integer values\n    # Assumes all input words are valid per problem description, no error handling required\n    int_values = [word_to_int[word] for word in words]\n\n    # Sort the list of integer values\n    int_values.sort()\n\n    # Convert the sorted integer values back to number words\n    sorted_words = [int_to_word[val] for val in int_values]\n\n    # Join the sorted words back into a space-delimited string\n    return \" \".join(sorted_words)"}
