{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the n-th Fib4 number iteratively using dynamic programming.\n    This function avoids recursion to efficiently calculate Fib4(n) in O(n) time and O(1) space.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0 or n == 1 or n == 3:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n\n    # Initialize the four previous values: fib4(k-4), fib4(k-3), fib4(k-2), fib4(k-1)\n    # For k=4, these correspond to fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n    # Iterate from k=4 up to the desired n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = a + b + c + d\n        # Shift values: a becomes b, b becomes c, c becomes d, d becomes next_fib\n        a, b, c, d = b, c, d, next_fib\n    \n    # After the loop, 'd' holds the value of fib4(n)\n    return d"}
