{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the n-th Fib4 number iteratively.\n    Uses a fixed-size buffer to achieve O(1) space complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the buffer with the first four sequence values\n    # representing fib4(n-4), fib4(n-3), fib4(n-2), fib4(n-1)\n    # When starting the loop for i=4, this buffer holds fib4(0) to fib4(3)\n    # [fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)]\n    last_four = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        # Calculate the next fib4 number\n        next_val = sum(last_four)\n        # Shift the buffer: remove the oldest value, add the new one\n        last_four.pop(0)\n        last_four.append(next_val)\n\n    # The last element in the buffer is fib4(n)\n    return last_four[-1]"}
