{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "    if len(l) < 2:\n        return True\n\n    # Determine initial direction by finding the first non-equal adjacent pair.\n    direction = None\n    for i in range(1, len(l)):\n        if l[i] > l[i - 1]:\n            direction = 1  # Increasing\n            break\n        elif l[i] < l[i - 1]:\n            direction = -1 # Decreasing\n            break\n\n    # If no change was found, all elements are equal, which is monotonic.\n    if direction is None:\n        return True\n\n    # Check if the list maintains the determined direction.\n    for i in range(1, len(l)):\n        # If the product is negative, the direction has changed.\n        # e.g., (2-1)*1 = 1 (ok); (1-2)*-1 = 1 (ok); (1-1)*1 = 0 (ok)\n        # but (1-2)*1 = -1 (not ok); (2-1)*-1 = -1 (not ok)\n        if (l[i] - l[i - 1]) * direction < 0:\n            return False\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "```python\ndef monotonic(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return True is list elements are monotonically increasing or decreasing.\"\"\"\n    if not l:\n        return True  # An empty list is considered monotonic\n\n    # Determine direction based on the first differing pair\n    direction = 0  # 0: unknown, 1: increasing, -1: decreasing\n    for i in range(1, len(l)):\n        diff = l[i] - l[i-1]\n        if diff > 0:\n            if direction == -1:  # Was decreasing, now increasing\n                return False\n            direction = 1\n        elif diff < 0:\n            if direction == 1:  # Was increasing, now decreasing\n                return False\n            direction = -1\n    return True\n```"}
