{"task_id": "HumanEval/67", "solution": "import re\n\ndef fruit_distribution(s,n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of mango fruits in a basket.\n    Extracts apple and orange counts from the string and subtracts them from the total.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Regex pattern to extract apple and orange counts\n    # The design context defines DESCRIPTION_PATTERN in utils.py\n    # r\"(?P<apples>\\d+)\\s+apples\\s+and\\s+(?P<oranges>\\d+)\\s+oranges\"\n    pattern = re.compile(r\"(?P<apples>\\d+)\\s+apples\\s+and\\s+(?P<oranges>\\d+)\\s+oranges\", re.IGNORECASE)\n    \n    match = pattern.fullmatch(s.strip())\n    \n    # Assuming valid input as per problem constraints, no explicit error handling for pattern mismatch\n    # Based on the design, an InvalidDescriptionError would be raised here,\n    # but the problem statement implies valid inputs for the examples.\n    apples = int(match.group(\"apples\"))\n    oranges = int(match.group(\"oranges\"))\n    \n    mangoes = n - apples - oranges\n    \n    return mangoes"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/67", "solution": "import re\n\ndef fruit_distribution(s,n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of mango fruits given a string description of apples and oranges\n    and the total number of fruits in the basket.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Define the regex pattern to extract apple and orange counts\n    DESCRIPTION_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"(\\d+)\\s+apples\\s+and\\s+(\\d+)\\s+oranges\")\n    \n    # Attempt to match the pattern in the input string\n    match = DESCRIPTION_PATTERN.fullmatch(s.strip())\n    \n    # Extract apple and orange counts; the problem statement implies valid input format.\n    apples = int(match.group(1))\n    oranges = int(match.group(2))\n    \n    # Calculate and return the number of mangoes\n    return n - apples - oranges"}
