{"task_id": "HumanEval/70", "solution": "def strange_sort_list(lst):\n    '''\n    Given list of integers, return list in strange order.\n    Strange sorting, is when you start with the minimum value,\n    then maximum of the remaining integers, then minimum and so on.\n    '''\n    sorted_lst = sorted(lst)\n    low, high = 0, len(sorted_lst) - 1\n    result = []\n\n    while low <= high:\n        result.append(sorted_lst[low])\n        low += 1\n        if low <= high:\n            result.append(sorted_lst[high])\n            high -= 1\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/70", "solution": "def strange_sort_list(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of integers in a strange order: min, then max, then next min, etc.\n    Achieves O(N log N) complexity by sorting initially and then using two pointers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return []\n\n    sorted_lst = sorted(lst)\n    result = []\n    left, right = 0, len(sorted_lst) - 1\n\n    while left <= right:\n        result.append(sorted_lst[left])\n        left += 1\n        if left <= right:\n            result.append(sorted_lst[right])\n            right -= 1\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/71", "solution": "import math\n\ndef triangle_area(a, b, c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the area of a triangle given its side lengths, or -1 if invalid.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate positive sides\n    if a <= 0 or b <= 0 or c <= 0:\n        return -1\n    \n    # Validate triangle inequality\n    if not (a + b > c and a + c > b and b + c > a):\n        return -1\n    \n    # Calculate semi-perimeter\n    s = (a + b + c) / 2\n    \n    # Calculate area using Heron's formula\n    area_squared = s * (s - a) * (s - b) * (s - c)\n    \n    # Due to floating point inaccuracies, area_squared might be very slightly negative for degenerate triangles.\n    # We should treat this as 0 or a valid small positive value.\n    if area_squared < 0:\n        area = 0.0\n    else:\n        area = math.sqrt(area_squared)\n    \n    return round(area, 2)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/71", "solution": "import math\n\ndef triangle_area(a, b, c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the area of a triangle given its three side lengths.\n    Returns the area rounded to 2 decimal places if valid, otherwise -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate if sides are positive\n    if not (a > 0 and b > 0 and c > 0):\n        return -1\n\n    # Validate triangle inequality theorem\n    if not (a + b > c and a + c > b and b + c > a):\n        return -1\n\n    # Calculate semi-perimeter\n    s = (a + b + c) / 2\n\n    # Calculate area using Heron's formula\n    # The term inside the square root should always be non-negative for a valid triangle,\n    # but due to floating point precision, it might be slightly negative, hence max(0, ...)\n    try:\n        area_squared = s * (s - a) * (s - b) * (s - c)\n        if area_squared < 0: # Handle potential small negative due to float precision\n            area = 0.0\n        else:\n            area = math.sqrt(area_squared)\n    except ValueError:\n        # This typically means area_squared was negative, which should not happen\n        # for a mathematically valid triangle, but could for edge cases or precision.\n        return -1 # Or handle as per specific error requirement. Design implies -1 for invalid.\n\n    return round(area, 2)"}
