{"task_id": "HumanEval/102", "solution": "def choose_num(x, y):\n    \"\"\"Returns the biggest even integer in the range [x, y], or -1 if none exists.\"\"\"\n    if x > y:\n        return -1\n    \n    # Find the largest even number less than or equal to y\n    max_even = y if y % 2 == 0 else y - 1\n    \n    # Check if this max_even is within the [x, y] range\n    if max_even >= x:\n        return max_even\n    else:\n        return -1"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/102", "solution": "```python\ndef choose_num(x, y):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the biggest even integer in the range [x, y] inclusive.\n    Returns -1 if no such number exists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if x > y:\n        return -1\n\n    if y % 2 == 0:\n        if y >= x:\n            return y\n        else:\n            return -1\n    else:\n        # y is odd, try y-1\n        if y - 1 >= x:\n            return y - 1\n        else:\n            return -1\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/103", "solution": "def rounded_avg(n, m):\n    \"\"\"Computes the average of integers from n through m, rounds to the nearest integer,\n    and converts the result to a binary string. Returns -1 if n > m.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n > m:\n        return -1\n\n    # The average of integers from n to m (inclusive) is simply (n + m) / 2.\n    # This avoids summing a potentially large range of numbers.\n    average = (n + m) / 2\n\n    # Round the average to the nearest integer. Python's round() uses banker's rounding.\n    rounded_value = round(average)\n\n    # Convert the rounded integer to its binary string representation.\n    return bin(rounded_value)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/103", "solution": "def rounded_avg(n, m):\n    \"\"\"Computes the rounded average of integers from n to m, converts it to binary.\"\"\"\n    if n > m:\n        return -1\n\n    # Calculate the sum of integers from n to m\n    # Using the arithmetic series sum formula: count * (first + last) / 2\n    count = m - n + 1\n    total = (n + m) * count // 2\n\n    avg = total / count\n    rounded = int(round(avg))\n\n    return bin(rounded)"}
