{"task_id": "HumanEval/136", "solution": "from typing import List, Optional, Tuple\n\ndef largest_smallest_integers(lst: List[int]) -> Tuple[Optional[int], Optional[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest negative integer and the smallest positive integer in a list.\n    Returns (largest_negative, smallest_positive) or (None, None) if not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    largest_neg: Optional[int] = None\n    smallest_pos: Optional[int] = None\n\n    for num in lst:\n        if num == 0:\n            continue\n\n        if num < 0:\n            if largest_neg is None or num > largest_neg:\n                largest_neg = num\n        else:  # num > 0\n            if smallest_pos is None or num < smallest_pos:\n                smallest_pos = num\n\n    return (largest_neg, smallest_pos)"}
