{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "def x_or_y(n, x, y):\n    \"\"\"A simple program which should return the value of x if n is \n    a prime number and should return the value of y otherwise.\n\n    Examples:\n    for x_or_y(7, 34, 12) == 34\n    for x_or_y(15, 8, 5) == 5\n    \n    \"\"\"\n    def is_prime(num):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a number is prime using trial division.\"\"\"\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        if num == 2 or num == 3:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        \n        i = 3\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 2\n        return True\n\n    if is_prime(n):\n        return x\n    else:\n        return y"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "def x_or_y(n, x, y):\n    \"\"\"Returns x if n is a prime number, and y otherwise.\"\"\"\n\n    def _is_prime(num):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a number is prime.\"\"\"\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        if num == 2:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 3\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 2\n        return True\n\n    if _is_prime(n):\n        return x\n    else:\n        return y"}
